    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "WIEL\nINFLIGHT\n™M\nStay connected to your world with Gogo.\nUse your laptop or any Wi-Fi enabled mobile device to access the Internet if\nyour flight is traveling over the continental United States. Log on and you can\nsurf the web, instant message, email and use your VPN-all at 30,000 feet.\nGogo Inflight Internet Availability\nSpokane\nSeattle O\nPontand o\nBoise\nReno/Lake Tahoe\nO Sacramento\nSan Fran J0900\nOLas Vegas\nLos Angeles O\nLong Beach\nrange Cosprings\n•Phoenix\n• San Diego\n•Tucson\nMinneapolis st Paule\nChicago (O'Hare)e\n• Denver\n•New York City/Newark\n• Washinoon, b.c. Keacan National\nAustin •\n•Dallas/Fort Worth\n• Houston\n• Miam\nAlaska\nInflight Internet service available\nInflight Internet service will be\navailable in early 2011\nAlaska Airlines.\ngogo\nInflight\nInternet\nPlease do not remove this card from aircraft\n2010.05",
      "WİFI\nINFLIGHT\nGogo Inflight Internet is now onboard.\nGET ONLINE IN 3 SIMPLE STEPS:\n1. Turn on your Wi-Fi\n2. Find the \"gogoinflight\" signal and connect\n3. Launch your browser and log in\nGive Gogo a go and enjoy free access to alaskaair.com\njust by opening up your Wi-Fi enabled device.\nNeed assistance or have questions about using Gogo?\nIn the air: airborne.gogoinflight.com | On the ground: gogoinflight.com\nCellular and Bluetooth® devices and voice services including Voice over Internet\nProtocol (VoIP) applications may not be used while in flight.\nGogo is available above 10,000 feet.\nAlaska Airlines®\ngogo\nInflight\nInternet\nPlease do not remove this card from aircraft\n©2010 Aircell, all rights reserved. Gogo is a registered trademark of Aircell LLC and its affiliates.\nAll other trademarks are the property of their respective owners. (10390)\n2010.180.007"
    ],
